  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════
       FAQ
  ═══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="ab-faq" aria-labelledby="ab-faq-h2">
    <div class="ab-faq-inner">
      <div class="ab-section-label">
        <span class="ab-label-dot">✦</span>
        <span>Common Questions</span>
      </div>
      <h2 class="ab-faq-h2" id="ab-faq-h2">What Chicagoland homeowners ask us most</h2>
      <div class="ab-faq-list">
        <details class="ab-faq-item">
          <summary class="ab-faq-q">Is All Masonry Services licensed and insured in Illinois?</summary>
          <p class="ab-faq-a">Yes. All Masonry Services Inc is fully licensed and insured for masonry work in Illinois. License numbers and Certificate of Insurance are available on request before any work begins.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="ab-faq-item">
          <summary class="ab-faq-q">Do you use subcontractors?</summary>
          <p class="ab-faq-a">Never. Every person who works on your property is a member of our own trained, licensed crew. We do not hire out work or use day-labor. This is non-negotiable at All Masonry Services.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="ab-faq-item">
          <summary class="ab-faq-q">How much does masonry work cost in Chicagoland?</summary>
          <p class="ab-faq-a">Costs vary significantly by service and scope. Tuckpointing typically runs $8–$20 per linear foot. Brick replacement runs $15–$45 per brick depending on material and access. Chimney repair starts at $400 and goes up with structural complexity. We provide written estimates after a free on-site inspection — no guessing.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="ab-faq-item">
          <summary class="ab-faq-q">How long does masonry repair take?</summary>
          <p class="ab-faq-a">Small tuckpointing or brick repair jobs typically complete in 1–2 days. Chimney rebuilds take 3–5 days. Large custom home masonry scopes are project-specific. We give you a realistic timeline in your written estimate.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="ab-faq-item">
          <summary class="ab-faq-q">What areas of Chicagoland do you serve?</summary>
          <p class="ab-faq-a">We serve the full Chicagoland area — including Hinsdale, Winnetka, Oak Brook, Naperville, Evanston, Arlington Heights, Schaumburg, Lake Forest, Barrington, Elmhurst, and the city of Chicago. In total we cover 19+ cities across the metro area.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="ab-faq-item">
          <summary class="ab-faq-q">When should I repair masonry — before or after winter?</summary>
          <p class="ab-faq-a">Before winter, if possible. Cracks and failed mortar joints allow water infiltration. When that water freezes, it expands and widens the damage every cycle. A repair that costs $300 in October can become a $3,000 structural repair by spring if left unchecked. We book fast in fall — schedule early.</p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

